2026-11-05 00:42:26 | Capabilities that REQUIRE a real multi-node production cluster (not testable on one workstation):
2026-11-05 00:42:26 |       P01  Permanent host loss with pod rescheduling onto another physical machine — Local-path PVs pin each Vertica pod to one node; production needs network/replicated CSI storage (EBS, Ceph, Portworx, vSAN) so the StatefulSet pod can restart elsewhere.
2026-11-05 00:42:26 |       P02  Kubernetes control-plane high availability — kind here has 1 control-plane; production uses 3+ control-plane nodes / managed K8s with an etcd quorum.
2026-11-05 00:42:26 |       P03  Zone / rack fault domains — Needs real failure domains with topologySpreadConstraints / zone labels; all 'nodes' here share one workstation.
2026-11-05 00:42:26 |       P04  Real network partitions, NIC/switch failures and latency between hosts — Simulated only by freezing a node container; real Spread heartbeat behaviour needs separate hosts.
2026-11-05 00:42:26 |       P05  Production performance and capacity benchmarks — All pods share the same CPU, RAM and SSD; numbers are relative, not sizing guidance.
2026-11-05 00:42:26 |       P06  Durable communal storage — A single MinIO pod on one disk is not durable; production uses S3 or an erasure-coded/replicated on-prem object store with TLS.
2026-11-05 00:42:26 |       P07  Off-site / cross-region disaster recovery — Requires a second cluster (VerticaReplicator CR or replicated object storage).
2026-11-05 00:42:26 |       P08  Metrics-driven autoscaling (VerticaAutoscaler + Prometheus/KEDA) and K8s node autoscaling — Needs a cluster autoscaler / cloud capacity; here scaling is triggered by CR changes.
2026-11-05 00:42:26 |       P09  Online rolling upgrade between Vertica releases (upgradePolicy: Online) — Needs a second, newer image version and production-sized subclusters.
2026-11-05 00:42:26 |       P10  Enterprise identity & secrets (LDAP/Kerberos, AWS Secrets Manager / Google Secret Manager, CA-signed certificates, etcd encryption at rest) — Requires corporate infrastructure; the lab uses Kubernetes Secrets and operator self-signed certificates.
2026-11-05 00:42:26 |       P11  Load balancers / ingress with real external IPs and DNS — Lab exposes NodePorts on 127.0.0.1 only.
2026-11-05 00:42:26 |       P12  Workload identity for communal storage (IRSA on Amazon EKS) — Vertica pods use their service-account JWT, exchanged through the cluster's OIDC provider for temporary S3 credentials, so no static access keys are stored (Vertica docs: IRSA profile authentication). Needs EKS and AWS IAM.
2026-11-05 00:42:26 |       P13  Production identity provider for OAuth 2.0 / JWT (Okta, OTDS, or Keycloak in production mode) — The lab Keycloak runs in dev mode (in-memory database, HTTP inside the cluster). Production: HTTPS endpoints, a highly available IdP, just-in-time user provisioning and role mapping from token claims.
